Guided Exercise: Manage Non-shared Storage with StatefulSets
Goal of This Lab
You perform two experiments:
1️⃣ Deployment (Shared Storage)
Deploy a web server and verify:
•	All pods share the same Persistent Volume
2️⃣ StatefulSet (Non-shared Storage)
Deploy MySQL database and verify:
•	Each pod gets its own Persistent Volume
________________________________________
PART 1 — Deploy Web Server with Shared Storage
Step 1: Login to OpenShift
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
Switch project:
oc project storage-statefulsets
________________________________________
Step 2: Create Deployment
Create a web server deployment
oc create deployment web-server \
--image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/hello-world-nginx:latest
Check deployment:
oc get deployment
Example output:
web-server   1/1   Running
________________________________________
Step 3: Add Persistent Volume
Create PVC and mount it in deployment.
oc set volumes deployment/web-server \
--add \
--name web-pv \
--type persistentVolumeClaim \
--claim-mode rwo \
--claim-size 5Gi \
--mount-path /usr/share/nginx/html \
--claim-name web-pv-claim
This command automatically:
•	Creates PVC
•	Creates PV (via storage class)
•	Mounts volume to container
Mount path:
/usr/share/nginx/html
This is where Nginx web content is stored.
________________________________________
Step 4: Verify Pod
List pods:
oc get pods -l app=web-server
Example:
web-server-5fb94fd568-48n8t
________________________________________
Step 5: Verify PVC
Check PVC:
oc get pvc
Example:
web-pv-claim   Bound   5Gi
Bound means:
PVC → connected to PV
________________________________________
Step 6: Verify Pod Uses PVC
Run:
oc get pod web-server-XXXXX -o json | jq .spec.volumes[0].persistentVolumeClaim.claimName
Output:
"web-pv-claim"
Meaning:
Pod → using web-pv-claim
________________________________________
Step 7: Add Data to PVC
Write content into shared storage.
oc exec -it pod/web-server-XXXXX -- /bin/bash -c \
'echo "Hello, World from ${HOSTNAME}" > /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html'
Now check content:
oc exec -it pod/web-server-XXXXX -- cat /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
Example:
Hello, World from web-server-5fb94fd568-48n8t
________________________________________
Step 8: Scale Deployment
Increase replicas:
oc scale deployment web-server --replicas 2
Check pods:
oc get pods
Example:
web-server-48n8t
web-server-rqvpb
________________________________________
Step 9: Verify Shared Storage
Check file in both pods.
Pod 1:
oc exec -it pod/web-server-48n8t -- cat /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
Pod 2:
oc exec -it pod/web-server-rqvpb -- cat /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
Both show:
Hello, World from web-server-48n8t
Meaning:
Both pods use SAME PV
Architecture:
Deployment
     │
 ┌───────┬───────┐
 │       │
Pod1    Pod2
 │       │
 └── Shared PV ──┘
________________________________________
PART 2 — Deploy Database Using StatefulSet
Now we deploy MySQL with StatefulSet.
Each pod will have its own storage.
________________________________________
Step 10: Create Headless Service
Edit file:
service-db.yml
Important line:
clusterIP: None
Full example:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: mysql-svc
spec:
  clusterIP: None
  selector:
    app: database
  ports:
  - port: 3306
Create service:
oc create -f service-db.yml
Verify:
oc get svc
You will see:
mysql-svc   ClusterIP   None
This is a Headless Service.
________________________________________
Step 11: Create StatefulSet
Edit file:
statefulset-db.yml
Important sections:
Replicas
replicas: 2
________________________________________
Volume Mount
volumeMounts:
- name: data
  mountPath: /var/lib/mysql
________________________________________
VolumeClaimTemplate
volumeClaimTemplates:
- metadata:
    name: data
  spec:
    accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
    storageClassName: "lvms-vg1"
    resources:
      requests:
        storage: 1Gi
This creates:
PVC for every pod automatically
________________________________________
Step 12: Create StatefulSet
oc create -f statefulset-db.yml
Check pods:
watch oc get pods -l app=database
Example:
dbserver-0
dbserver-1
Notice:
Ordered pod names
________________________________________
Step 13: Verify Endpoints
oc get endpoints
Example:
mysql-svc   10.8.0.112:3306,10.8.0.113:3306
These are the pod IPs.
________________________________________
Step 14: Test Pod DNS
StatefulSet pods get stable DNS.
Format:
podname.servicename
Example:
dbserver-1.mysql-svc
Test:
oc rsh dbserver-1 curl -v telnet://dbserver-1.mysql-svc:3306
DNS resolves directly to dbserver-1.
________________________________________
Step 15: Verify PVCs
Run:
oc get pvc -l app=database
Output:
data-dbserver-0
data-dbserver-1
Each pod has its own PVC.
Architecture:
StatefulSet
      │
 ┌───────────┬───────────┐
 │           │
dbserver-0  dbserver-1
 │           │
PVC0        PVC1
 │           │
PV0         PV1
________________________________________
Step 16: Verify PVC Used by Each Pod
Check pod 0:
oc get pod dbserver-0 -o json | jq .spec.volumes[0].persistentVolumeClaim.claimName
Output:
data-dbserver-0
Check pod 1:
data-dbserver-1
________________________________________
Step 17: Add Database Tables
Pod 0:
oc exec -it pod/dbserver-0 -- /bin/bash -c \
"mysql -uredhat -predhat123 sakila -e 'create table items (count INT);'"
Pod 1:
oc exec -it pod/dbserver-1 -- /bin/bash -c \
"mysql -uredhat -predhat123 sakila -e 'create table inventory (count INT);'"
________________________________________
Step 18: Verify Data is Different
Check pod 0:
show tables;
Output:
items
Check pod 1:
inventory
Meaning:
Pods DO NOT share storage
________________________________________
Step 19: Delete Pod
Delete pod:
oc delete pod dbserver-0
Check pods:
oc get pods
New pod appears:
dbserver-0
________________________________________
Step 20: Verify Data Persists
Check tables again:
show tables;
Output:
items
Meaning:
PVC preserved data
Even though pod was deleted.
________________________________________
Final Comparison (VERY IMPORTANT)
Feature	Deployment	StatefulSet
Storage	Shared	Separate
Pod Names	Random	Ordered
PVC	Single	One per pod
Use Case	Web apps	Databases
________________________________________
Final Architecture
Deployment
web-server deployment
        │
   ┌─────────┬─────────┐
   │         │
pod1       pod2
   │         │
   └── Shared PV ──┘
________________________________________
StatefulSet
dbserver statefulset
        │
   ┌─────────┬─────────┐
   │         │
dbserver-0  dbserver-1
   │         │
 PVC0       PVC1
   │         │
 PV0        PV1
________________________________________
